[0] Scientific research and technological innovation support one another and can profoundly change methods of investigation and production. Astronomy is an ancient science, and space technology makes it possible to observe the universe from beyond Earth's atmosphere.
Molecular biology and genetics have advanced the study of life processes, while progress in chemistry has expanded the chemical industry's ability to synthesize and produce substances. Geology, meteorology, oceanography and other natural sciences also develop through new theories, instruments and methods.
[1] Technologies for energy, materials, production and infrastructure continue to develop. Changes in electricity generation include using nuclear energy alongside the combustion of fossil fuels, rather than an inevitable conversion of every fossil-fuel power station to a nuclear plant.
Materials science enables the manufacture of materials with particular useful properties, and mechanization and automation have changed many industrial and agricultural processes. Technological improvements also provide ways to improve the efficiency and performance of transport, construction and communication.
