[3] Scientific and technological progress can support large-scale improvements in production. Turning knowledge into reliable equipment, processes and infrastructure can help meet society's material needs.
The social effects of these improvements depend on how people organize and use technology;
they are not automatically guaranteed by a political system or by technological development itself.
