[6] Neutrinos can carry information from stellar interiors, and observations of solar neutrinos help investigate nuclear reactions in the Sun's core. Their interpretation must also account for neutrinos changing type as they travel.
Nuclear and particle physics provide the theoretical and experimental foundations for neutrino detection. Neutrino astronomy has not settled whether macroscopic worlds made of antiparticles exist, and the universe's matter-antimatter asymmetry remains a subject of research.
