[13] Controlled nuclear fusion has the potential to supply energy, but it cannot guarantee that humanity will never face energy problems again. Turning fusion reactions into reliable electricity generation requires solutions for sustaining the reaction, using its energy, materials and engineering.
Nuclear physics provides a scientific foundation for both fission and fusion energy. Practical power systems also need support from other fields of physics and engineering.
