[14] **Modern technology can use materials whose properties are designed for particular purposes**, but these materials still require material feedstocks and do not eliminate the use of natural resources. Material synthesis and processing allow properties to be adjusted to technological needs.
Physical methods using electron beams, ion beams, laser beams, strong magnetic fields, high pressure, high temperature and ultrasound can be combined with chemical methods to prepare or treat suitable materials. They can produce particular material properties and new ways of processing materials, thereby improving production processes.
