[15] Many production processes in industry and agriculture can be automated. Automated systems measure the state of a process and use electronic controls to adjust equipment operation.
Measuring, monitoring and control instruments provide the information and means needed for this operation. Their design draws on radio electronics, solid-state physics and other fields of physics, while some measurement methods also use results from nuclear physics.
