[16] Physics provides an important foundation for electronic computing. Early electronic computers are commonly grouped into three generations according to their main devices: vacuum tubes, transistors and integrated circuits①. This historical classification does not mean that computer development ended there.
Physical research on devices and materials helps reduce circuit size and improve computational speed and reliability. Laser technology and holographic techniques, which use coherent light to record and reconstruct optical information, also provide approaches for research in optical information processing and related computing technologies. This does not establish that they will generally replace electronic circuits.
