[17] ① An integrated circuit forms many electronic components and their connections on a small chip, instead of linking a collection of separate components one by one with external wires. Manufacturing can change local semiconductor properties by introducing impurity atoms and can also form and pattern thin films on the surface.
These steps produce devices with particular structures and electrical functions. They cannot simply be described as layers of a particular kind of molecule. Miniaturization can put part of a radio's circuitry on a chip the size of a match head, but the chip is not a complete radio with its antenna, power supply and other components.
