[19] Understanding the basic laws of nature, especially through physics, helps people understand technology and continue developing science and engineering. Applying this knowledge to practical problems provides means to improve production and meet human needs.
Technological capability by itself does not determine how society distributes goods or guarantee the realization of a particular social ideal.
